# ── Backend origin (development only) ──
# Used by the /api proxy in next.config.ts. In development the frontend runs on
# :3000 and the API on :8000; proxying through Next keeps the browser on a single
# origin so the httpOnly auth cookies are actually sent.
#
# Read at BUILD time, not at start time: `next build` writes the destination into
# .next/routes-manifest.json and `next start` reads it back from there. Setting this
# only for `next start` has no effect. A stale value in your shell will be compiled
# into the build and silently point the proxy at the wrong port.
#
# Ignored on Vercel, where vercel.json routes /api to the backend service instead.
BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8000
